IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja2-part5-ca-general`

-- Tests for the Court of Appeal general module (ss 48 to 52). Expected values are written from the text of the sections, not from the code.

`test: Judge J1` MEANS Judge WITH
    `reference for this person` IS "J1"
    office IS `Judge of the High Court`
    `date of appointment` IS Date 1 1 2010

`test: Judge J2` MEANS Judge WITH
    `reference for this person` IS "J2"
    office IS `Justice of the Court of Appeal`
    `date of appointment` IS Date 1 1 2005

GIVEN for IS A NUMBER, against IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Split of opinion`
`test: a split of` MEANS `Split of opinion` WITH
    `Judges for the claim, appeal or application` IS for
    `Judges against it` IS against

-- s 48(1): the Chief Justice is the President of the Court of Appeal and may appoint Vice-Presidents from among the Justices of the Court of Appeal
#ASSERT (`s 48(1) the Judge is the President of the Court of Appeal` `Chief Justice`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 48(1) the Judge is the President of the Court of Appeal` `Judge of the High Court`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 48(1) the Chief Justice may appoint the Judge to be a Vice-President of the Court of Appeal` `Justice of the Court of Appeal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 48(1) the Chief Justice may appoint the Judge to be a Vice-President of the Court of Appeal` `Judge of the High Court`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 48(2)(a) and (b): the most senior Supreme Court Judge presides; if there is no Supreme Court Judge the Chief Justice appoints a person to preside
#ASSERT (`s 48(2)(a) the Judge is to preside in a sitting of the Court of Appeal` `test: Judge J2` (JUST `test: Judge J2`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 48(2)(a) the Judge is to preside in a sitting of the Court of Appeal` `test: Judge J1` (JUST `test: Judge J2`)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 48(2)(a) the Judge is to preside in a sitting of the Court of Appeal` `test: Judge J1` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 48(2)(b) the Chief Justice is to appoint a person to preside in a sitting of the Court of Appeal` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 48(2)(b) the Chief Justice is to appoint a person to preside in a sitting of the Court of Appeal` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 49(1): the civil, the criminal and the Division 4 jurisdiction
#ASSERT (`s 49(1) the Court of Appeal has jurisdiction over the matter` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 49(1) the Court of Appeal has jurisdiction over the matter` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 49(1) the Court of Appeal has jurisdiction over the matter` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 49(1) the Court of Appeal has jurisdiction over the matter` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 49(1) the Court of Appeal has jurisdiction over the matter` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 49(2): in an appeal and for any purpose relating to an appeal, all the jurisdiction and powers of the court or tribunal from which the appeal was brought
#ASSERT (`s 49(2) the Court of Appeal has the jurisdiction or power of the court or tribunal from which the appeal was brought` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 49(2) the Court of Appeal has the jurisdiction or power of the court or tribunal from which the appeal was brought` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 49(2) the Court of Appeal has the jurisdiction or power of the court or tribunal from which the appeal was brought` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 49(3): may decide any question that needs to be decided to do justice in any case before it
#ASSERT (`s 49(3) the Court of Appeal may decide the question` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 49(3) the Court of Appeal may decide the question` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 49(3) the Court of Appeal may decide the question` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 50(1): "3 or any greater uneven number of Judges"
#ASSERT (`s 50(1) the number of Judges is one that the subsection provides for` 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 50(1) the number of Judges is one that the subsection provides for` 5) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 50(1) the number of Judges is one that the subsection provides for` 4) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 50(1) the number of Judges is one that the subsection provides for` 2) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 50(1) the number of Judges is one that the subsection provides for` 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 50(2): "A Judge must not sit ... to hear or decide any appeal from a decision made by the Judge, or any matter related to such an appeal."
#ASSERT (`s 50(2) the Judge may sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide the matter` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 50(2) the Judge may sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide the matter` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 50(2) the Judge may sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide the matter` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 50(3): section 10A applies to this court as it applies to the General Division; the answer is passed through
#ASSERT (`s 50(3) the Court of Appeal may summon assessors as section 10A allows` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 50(3) the Court of Appeal may summon assessors as section 10A allows` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 50(3) the Court of Appeal may summon assessors as section 10A allows` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 51(1): "in accordance with the opinion of the majority of the Judges hearing the case"
#ASSERT (`s 51(1) the decision goes the way of the opinion of the majority of the Judges hearing the case` (`test: a split of` 2 1)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 51(1) the decision goes the way of the opinion of the majority of the Judges hearing the case` (`test: a split of` 1 2)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 51(1) the decision goes the way of the opinion of the majority of the Judges hearing the case` (`test: a split of` 1 1)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 51(2): "to be dismissed if the Judges hearing the appeal or application are evenly divided"
#ASSERT (`s 51(2) the appeal or application is dismissed because the Judges hearing it are evenly divided` (`test: a split of` 1 1)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 51(2) the appeal or application is dismissed because the Judges hearing it are evenly divided` (`test: a split of` 2 1)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 51(2) the appeal or application is dismissed because the Judges hearing it are evenly divided` (`test: a split of` 0 2)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 52(1)(a): sits on such dates and at such places as the Chief Justice may appoint
#ASSERT (`s 52(1)(a) the date is one that the Chief Justice appointed` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 52(1)(a) the date is one that the Chief Justice appointed` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 52(1)(a) the place is one that the Chief Justice appointed` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 52(1)(a) the place is one that the Chief Justice appointed` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 52(1)(b): may sit on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, or during a vacation, if the Chief Justice so appoints
#ASSERT (`s 52(1)(b) the Court of Appeal may sit on the day` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 52(1)(b) the Court of Appeal may sit on the day` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 52(1)(b) the Court of Appeal may sit on the day` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 52(1)(b) the Court of Appeal may sit on the day` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 52(2): the Chief Justice may cancel or postpone a sitting appointed under subsection (1)
#ASSERT (`s 52(2) the Chief Justice may cancel or postpone the sitting` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 52(2) the Chief Justice may cancel or postpone the sitting` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
